+
+**The stock-take of 2 November 2026 (decisions ST-1 to ST-5).** At the owner's request the three chats and the owner compared their understanding of how the finished system will behave. The record is `exchange/STOCKTAKE_2026_11_02_v0_8.md` (`fd4bee1`; LF `87cbe55cb50b3ad8727ac2693125e922645b665a832650b751285519b7a9ed18`): the owner's part (d), his own picture of the system after implementation (also committed by him as `owner_stocktake_v1_0.txt`, `f47ce14`; the owner's own text, not reviewed); the new chat's answers (`exchange/Stocktake_answers_from_Claude_v0_2.md`, `c13ffcd`); the reviewer chat's Response 2; the previous chat's Responses 3 and 3b; and the new chat's Response 4. **The owner ratified on 2 November 2026 (22:44 Adelaide)** the positions below, as the record's last section states; they fixed the owner's inputs to the Mode H design and authorised no run:
+- **ST-1 (frozen records):** the three-way split: a frozen forecast is never changed; an accepted score is kept and any new scoring run is added beside it, never over it; a league table is a view, so adding or retiring a method gives a new dated report while every earlier report stays as published. A retired revision is archived and indexed: its code and tests go to the archive and its registry entry becomes RETIRED, while its forecasts and scores stay where they are with an index pointing at them. Three labels: PROSPECTIVE, CATCH-UP and development evidence. Response 3b is the reading of the owner's part (d).
+- **ST-2 (carried into the design):** the previous chat's Response 3 section 4, with Response 4's additions: nothing is ever scored twice; a draw whose result is not yet accepted is left open, never skipped; the weekly command prints a status block per game; at most one open forecast per variant per game. **Current interpretation (EX_134 C02; the owner's wording above is kept as history):** "nothing is ever scored twice" means that no duplicate routine accepted score is produced for a forecast under the same scoring contract. A newly identified scoring run for a corrected scorer or a new measure is permitted under ST-1, preserves the earlier accepted score, and has its own identity and provenance (as the direction document says, section 5 step 3). This permits no re-scoring of any real run now.
+- **ST-3 (recommendations):** Response 3 section 5 as amended by Response 4 section 3: Q1 preference A with the honest wording, B kept as the alternative for the reviewer's R-3 review, C withdrawn; Q5 by a local install record (a one-off record for the cohort released on 31 October 2026, confirmed by the owner); the first design (EX_123) revised and cold-read before it went to the reviewer; the cross-batch report after WF-1C.
+- **ST-4:** the previous Claude chat retired on 2 November 2026.
+- **ST-5 (planning target):** Mode H and the weekly session installed by about 13 to 15 November 2026, so the first forecasts frozen before a draw are Oz Lotto 1709 (Tuesday 17 November) and Powerball 1592 (Thursday 19 November); the week of 9 November a stretch only. FB-1 applies: the schedule slips rather than any review or rehearsal being cut.
+- **Correction (3 November 2026; the record's correction note):** the reason the stock-take gave for withdrawing option C, "no released method uses its target's draw number", is wrong as stated. The target is not a scientific input of any released method, but it enters every method's tie-break key (`src/methods/_common/contract_records.py` lines 405-409), every non-legacy view digest (`game_draws_reader.py` line 125) and E_1's own tie key (`E_001/multigame_e1.py` lines 23 and 50). The corrected reason: under C the ten forecasts from one training prefix would have identical scores and could differ only in the order of tied numbers, so C would test one scoring ten times. The withdrawal stands.
